---
code: mark-brace-verdict-single-cell
when-fires: a brace-alternation `@{a,b}` appears on a single-cell verdict/observe mark. oracle/predict/derive.rs. Static (literal braces escaped in the template).
why: 277 §4c: a verdict/observe mark asserts exactly one cell; the brace mints no cell and the site runs (a role-aware rejection the parser cannot make).
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# One rc cannot witness two cells, so the alternation has nothing to expand into here.
hork__predict() {
   hork --query "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Package:"$1"@{installed,pinned}
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
